    "blurb": "Manage Couchbase documents from Camunda",
    "overview": "Manage documents and run N1QL or SQL++ queries directly from BPMN processes with secure outbound integration.",
    "rating": null,
    "reviewCount": 0,
    "mobileBundleId": null,
    "mobileAppStoreId": null
  },
  "overview": {
    "splashTitle": "Integrate Couchbase document operations and queries into Camunda processes",
    "splashDescription": "This connector supports document retrieval, upsert, replace, and delete operations, and it can execute N1QL or SQL++ queries directly from BPMN without requiring a custom job worker. The connector includes operational guardrails for production use, including optional TLS enforcement, connection pooling, configurable query timeout, positional query parameters, scan consistency control, automatic LIMIT protection, and an optional SELECT-only policy to prevent accidental mutations from process data. Authentication is handled through a Couchbase connection string, username, and password, and the README recommends using Camunda secrets for those values. The connector includes operational guardrails for production use, including optional TLS enforcement, connection pooling, configurable query timeout, positional query parameters, scan consistency control, automatic LIMIT protection, and an optional SELECT-only policy to prevent accidental mutations from process data. Authentication is handled through a Couchbase connection string, username, and password, and the README recommends using Camunda secrets for those values.",
    "imageUrl": "https://d3bql97l1ytoxn.cloudfront.net/app_resources/836163/overview/img16291732647902126787.png?d91da5ebc491c188ef97bf5b3b880798",
